    {
      "type": "Block",
      "value": "---\nesid: sec-Intl.Locale.prototype.getCalendars\ndescription: >\n  When the locale has no region, the Add Likely Subtags algorithm is used to\n  derive the region whose calendar preference is returned.\ninfo: |\n  RegionPreference ( locale )\n  ...\n  2. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n    a. Set _region_ to CanonicalUnicodeSubdivision(_locale_, *\"sd\"*).\n    b. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n      i. Let _maximal_ be the result of the Add Likely Subtags algorithm applied\n         to _locale_. If an error is signaled, set _maximal_ to _locale_.\n      ii. Set _maximal_ to CanonicalizeUnicodeLocaleId(_maximal_).\n      iii. Set _region_ to GetLocaleRegion(_maximal_).\n      iv. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n        1. Set _region_ to *\"001\"*.\n  ...\nfeatures: [Intl.Locale, Intl.Locale-info]\n---",
      "start": 124,
      "end": 927
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " In order not to rely on a particular implementation's locale data, this test",
      "start": 929,
      "end": 1008
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " searches for a suitable locale without a region subtag, but where the likely",
      "start": 1009,
      "end": 1088
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " region would influence the supported calendars.",
      "start": 1089,
      "end": 1139
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 1140,
      "end": 1142
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Each candidate below is a language subtag together with the region that the",
      "start": 1143,
      "end": 1221
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Add Likely Subtags algorithm derives for it (e.g. \"th\" maximizes to",
      "start": 1222,
      "end": 1292
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " \"th-Thai-TH\", so \"th-TH\"). A language tag without a region, subdivision (\"sd\"",
      "start": 1293,
      "end": 1373
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " keyword), or region override (\"rg\" keyword) passed to RegionPreference must",
      "start": 1374,
      "end": 1452
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " apply Add Likely Subtags and arrive at the paired region. Its calendars must",
      "start": 1453,
      "end": 1532
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " therefore be identical to those of the candidate locale. An incorrect",
      "start": 1533,
      "end": 1605
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " implementation might instead fall back to the region \"001\" in step 2.b.iv.",
      "start": 1606,
      "end": 1683
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 1684,
      "end": 1686
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " We could assume even less about the locale data by not hardcoding these",
      "start": 1687,
      "end": 1761
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " likely regions and instead checking all available locales with the result of",
      "start": 1762,
      "end": 1841
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " maximize() on each one, but that assumes the implementation has a working",
      "start": 1842,
      "end": 1918
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " maximize(), and if that's the case then it probably implements this step",
      "start": 1919,
      "end": 1994
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " correctly as well.",
      "start": 1995,
      "end": 2016
    }
  ],
